* ============================================================================
* memo_edges_probe.dts -- first in-house batch of AIF-108 challenge ideas,
* the CLI-reachable payload/lifecycle edges (challenge M2: "run every [NOW]
* idea in-house first -- we do not open a challenge on ground we have not
* walked"). Covers ideas 1 (empty payload), 2 (one byte), 12 (update longer;
* append-new), 13 (update shorter; no truncation), and the clear/reinsert
* cycle. Binary-payload ideas (NULs, high bytes) are NOT reachable from CLI
* string literals -- those stay for harness-tier submissions, stated plainly.
*
* Self-bootstrapping in the RAM VFS, self-erasing. Markers by field value.
* PROBE tier: promoted to a regression only after a maintainer green.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

DO mem
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO mem

FORMULA "MEMO-EDGES-BEGIN"

CREATE X64 MEDGES (ID N(4,0), NOTES M)
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1

* --- idea 1: empty payload round-trip ---------------------------------------
REPLACE NOTES WITH ""
CLOSE
USE MEDGES
? "ME_T1_empty_roundtrip:" + (NOTES = "")

* --- idea 2: one byte --------------------------------------------------------
REPLACE NOTES WITH "X"
CLOSE
USE MEDGES
? "ME_T2_one_byte:" + (NOTES = "X")

* --- idea 12: update longer (append-new semantics observable at CLI tier) ---
REPLACE NOTES WITH "a considerably longer payload than one byte, easily"
CLOSE
USE MEDGES
? "ME_T3_update_longer:" + (NOTES = "a considerably longer payload than one byte, easily")

* --- idea 13: update shorter (no truncation artifacts) -----------------------
REPLACE NOTES WITH "short"
CLOSE
USE MEDGES
? "ME_T4_update_shorter:" + (NOTES = "short")

* --- clear then reinsert (the canary's third act, on the edge table) ---------
REPLACE NOTES WITH ""
REPLACE NOTES WITH "after the clear"
CLOSE
USE MEDGES
? "ME_T5_clear_reinsert:" + (NOTES = "after the clear")

FORMULA "MEMO-EDGES-END"

VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
